    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented for the \"reject duplicate email with 409\" rule, following the same pattern as the existing telephone-uniqueness check:\n\n1. **`RequireUniqueEmail`** function \u2014 runs in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline after `RequireOwnerFields` (which lower-cases the email). It compares the request's lower-cased email against every existing owner's lower-cased email and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a match. Requests without an email are skipped.\n\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, mirroring the telephone handler.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n\n5. Wired the new `uniqueEmail` step into `owners.POST.yml` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`), between the telephone and household uniqueness checks.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass.",
